  "notes": "Allow a bounded CRT address-safety retry after a deferred initialization attempt.\n\nPreviously, initialization attempts=1 excluded Deferred/AddressUnsafe from both automatic quarantine release and the separate address-proof path. A connected CRT could therefore remain held in XSHUT after a transient startup condition. Initialization attempts no longer consume that independent proof opportunity.\n\nThe existing limits remain: at most three address-proof passes in a nonrenewable five-second window with 250 ms retry delay. Window/BusBusy still require no prior initialization attempt. Confirmed missing/functional faults, cancellation and other excluded reasons remain blocked. Bus ownership, XSHUT settling, primary-address proof, CRT model identity and the possible-default-address latch are not waived. Future retry deadlines are preserved.\n\nConnected-device readback reached normal Desktop/Twin with CRT Ready on its first initialization attempt, no new HAL timeout, and unchanged 64-row flashlight learning. The exact post-attempt retry case is verified by a compiled production-policy regression test and review; this boot did not reproduce that intermittent branch. Primary IR and heater-NTC faults remain. The prior cooler-reference fix still reports a measured but inconclusive result, without a false health PASS.\n\nValidation: fresh review, 44 host suites, checked ESP32-S3 build, actual ELF/map deadline audit, exact USB END/hash acknowledgement and guarded target readback. Static RAM unchanged. Firmware: 3166096 bytes; SHA-256 ceba4522e7c91489bda36ac76951829c6f49fecbb4e28f0d6da5a6bfac13672b. Full QA remains incomplete.\n",
